mastery.question_text:
Two items were each bought for $\$2400$.
Their values over $n$ years are shown.
State what the intercept means for both items, and say which curve models an item that is gaining value.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=8cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.5,xmax=6.8,ymin=-300,ymax=5000,xtick={0,1,...,6},ytick={0,600,...,4800},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$n$},ylabel={Value (\$)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,->,domain=0:6.3,samples=100] {2400*exp(x*ln(1.1))} node[pos=0.75,above left] {$A$};
\addplot[thick,red,dashed,->,domain=0:6.5,samples=100] {2400*exp(x*ln(0.9))} node[pos=0.75,below left] {$B$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

